    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "860ca79c_5f5d6e93",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-23T21:13:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intention was to actually Not Support any extended messages, although I may have missed something.\n\nNot Supporting extended messages entirely appears to be basically spec compliant (with the caveat that devices with batteries are required to support Get Battery Cap and Get Battery Status). If we support extended messages, we are required to support chunking.",
      "parentUuid": "aa73c1e3_a5a4a34a",
      "revId": "94076486f5876b7a3085e6a01cea82f3371dde30",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7d666f9_d194821d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-23T21:27:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the spec, we need to support the extended battery cap message. Page 228, Table 6-67 Applicability of Extended Messages.\n\nThe table sets Extended Battery Cap message to CN1 for Transmit and CN4 for Receive.\n\nCN – Conditional Normative ; Shall be supported by a given Port/Cable Plug based on features\n\nNote 1: Shall be supported by products that contain batteries.\nNote 4: Shall be supported by products that can transmit the Get_Battery_Cap Message.",
      "parentUuid": "860ca79c_5f5d6e93",
      "revId": "94076486f5876b7a3085e6a01cea82f3371dde30",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
